#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/id #uuid "87bf279f-9f78-54cb-b9c3-e1bf1c5426ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-4505" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/cdadd8a9c68f58c4d8434e658d4acffeba524850f361fcd3d6fe3524b3d781a1.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/35104266eb5a086bef0536640ec1310532cc136a251049a1adcfe4418ef0ef89.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/aa4de061ca95088763e7e5fec289dbd2e5bd298e8986ef6660617ea0ba227821.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/10781c0f9183c793e3f2de287ede937e764d942767ecc9b64942dc338c1e1307.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114980 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "359f4b72-60d2-54e2-b7ef-c48f1e3af708" :question/math-academy-id "e-4506" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5y=-3x \\\\ 6+x=-2+y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y=0 \\\\ x-y=-8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/648952bc6e093c08ff29215fce21fe115ab81e9fc3d8b423772123eae31237f3.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/c1f203be0770c298d9c2c75ccfbfb30354cb314ed75c8b05f6639e5633ca7442.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/aa4de061ca95088763e7e5fec289dbd2e5bd298e8986ef6660617ea0ba227821.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/75aed8c54a2ec274def967802cbd3b67d0fad3358e676b02cf52e1e8d2cbe0d7.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114981 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b87aa5eb-f689-5f34-baeb-f97c3f200552" :question/math-academy-id "e-4507" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052302/assets/6f0ddb43928e0d9f52ca2fe0f0ab578adfa986cba8179746bd34a50a1a7c506b.png)" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x-15y=5 \\\\ 1x+0y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=1 \\\\ x=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95911773-a2b9-59dc-acda-1e9feb02e982" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329817} {:answer/id #uuid "6575d615-5ee4-538e-b83f-d4d07b29f21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329818} {:answer/id #uuid "65ab39fb-8796-53b1-918f-21ff6d859495" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329819} {:answer/id #uuid "209a7be1-d08b-57f4-a565-edb3f452c8d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329820} {:answer/id #uuid "2ab79c24-cea4-5450-936c-c5a0abfe4945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65ab39fb-8796-53b1-918f-21ff6d859495" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329819} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4a0eb64-dfb3-56d5-ac46-ccd6c7310508" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14a1aab2-ba6f-5609-9711-81f9e6143453" :question/math-academy-id "q-12291" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x=y-1 \\\\ x=-y+1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-y=-1 \\\\ x+y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "625665e9-aa08-59df-99d0-705510c1021e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329824} {:answer/id #uuid "56756f75-7581-5b38-aea7-bedf594ab09e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329825} {:answer/id #uuid "7353a03a-e31b-5c57-9998-fcd14a65274f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329826} {:answer/id #uuid "768797d5-c251-59a2-8b56-918782a6129d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329827} {:answer/id #uuid "6063575f-6e09-59a1-83af-38dcd8fe4c1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "768797d5-c251-59a2-8b56-918782a6129d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329827} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4123b0-8bc5-5bbf-a629-3fe41cdb8276" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9ac1a19-67e1-5b9e-a25e-dce563843083" :question/math-academy-id "q-130501" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=4 \\\\ x-y=-10\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=4 \\\\ x-y=-10\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcc7b819-d34d-5e43-95c9-c1b281f2d4c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285569} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc182d2-9706-5763-93dc-587dab323cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285570} {:answer/id #uuid "623abe45-ff87-5e43-9dc1-245c2962faf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+5y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285571} {:answer/id #uuid "baa1cfed-e269-547a-9c12-2e3d7b76faa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=-15 \\\\ 12x+6y=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285572} {:answer/id #uuid "5674977b-88eb-5d70-9612-43da6db8de1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=15 \\\\ 4x+y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dc182d2-9706-5763-93dc-587dab323cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285570} :answer-field/id #uuid "d80dc95a-ccfe-5c63-add0-c28ed2aa747c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dad4c0b-b40d-5232-bf24-f4b25c943bdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-130523" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 25 \\\\ 12 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+25y=15 \\\\ 12x+3y=-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y=3 \\\\ 4x+y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329829 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6fb7b69-5f5f-5a90-929c-86fe93404cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6fb7b69-5f5f-5a90-929c-86fe93404cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329831} :answer-field/id #uuid "857eb249-ad8b-5167-a8b1-b35d4c144ad8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c94a36-e484-5ceb-9995-66292cc8fe0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24c94a36-e484-5ceb-9995-66292cc8fe0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329833} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd57cfe2-d61b-51e7-973b-d2efc23c5d25" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d84d7eb9-aa25-54fe-9c40-b230a780c2cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d84d7eb9-aa25-54fe-9c40-b230a780c2cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329835} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c4cd0cb-e99c-5756-9de3-12a67f415b56" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158e6771-9e67-5283-bccb-51803c54845d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158e6771-9e67-5283-bccb-51803c54845d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329837} :answer-field/id #uuid "af264061-7716-56ee-ac3c-18bb07f83d0b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8a84340-963d-5015-a9d9-2f93ab0b6c20" :question/math-academy-id "q-275612" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-4y+3x=8 \\\\ 2x=-3,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | $8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $8$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y=8 \\\\ 2x+0y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285598 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer