e\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f746a1-ea9e-5136-90d6-d4dee1306c17" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product by Reorganizing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0d1cb97-6c3b-5b01-a60c-e61207979561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0d1cb97-6c3b-5b01-a60c-e61207979561" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329852} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bfd3682-72a2-5cb3-bfe6-9aad82f358c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fbbd8cc-fef9-5efa-9072-b243a92b1551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fbbd8cc-fef9-5efa-9072-b243a92b1551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329854} :answer-field/id #uuid "4feea498-6993-54f7-a01f-336026cf9564" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c072006b-b11e-5501-b759-3220c266e025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c072006b-b11e-5501-b759-3220c266e025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329856} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8fc4be3-ff8b-5dd1-8693-7b33333d6d66" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329855} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49096ef0-5562-5e0c-8b37-506a3570d605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49096ef0-5562-5e0c-8b37-506a3570d605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329858} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9871a2-a512-57ce-aac7-21ba2ca7dbdb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329857}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "37090c7a-4776-5826-957a-cbe6e7e03bab" :question/math-academy-id "q-317540" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4=x \\\\ -7=3+y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | $1$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-10$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-10$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+0y=4 \\\\ 0x+y=-10\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35ed4af9-f1ad-551e-8ca5-9226fc685adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35ed4af9-f1ad-551e-8ca5-9226fc685adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329861} :answer-field/id #uuid "445dd686-95d4-521f-9f83-4d44948006fc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd1d4367-60c8-5504-b0cf-505cf1453fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd1d4367-60c8-5504-b0cf-505cf1453fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329863} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cc097c3-0457-5183-97a8-f2f2ccb8ab80" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3f153ac-5333-502d-8f7a-6d527498b0b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-317563" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $\\,4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,3.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix encodes the coefficients of $x$ and $y$, and the $2\\times 1$ vector on the right gives the constants, so the system is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8x-4y=16 \\\\ -6x+12y=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the first equation by $4$ and the second by $-6$ gives the simplified system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=4 \\\\ x-2y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the entries shown above."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd7ce83e-518a-5f4c-a220-cee58da5a351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329866} {:answer/id #uuid "06b5f7ff-79b5-5ecd-85a1-cefa0220ff5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd7ce83e-518a-5f4c-a220-cee58da5a351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329866} :answer-field/id #uuid "55333ffd-3e8c-507c-8240-9854e5fd5fb8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329865} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78f4d578-4394-5d5b-be75-6d73308ece84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78f4d578-4394-5d5b-be75-6d73308ece84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329869} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ab8b6bd-47e4-5850-9db0-d0e306133f57" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66a12d9b-426b-5ec9-ab6f-48275c2490ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-317570" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=11 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d356e6d9-2f05-51ee-a259-073969094204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329872}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d356e6d9-2f05-51ee-a259-073969094204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329872} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c638c59-e340-5dbe-984f-08f55dad2115" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e6fb009-90d6-59ee-9108-0f0192ccb211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e6fb009-90d6-59ee-9108-0f0192ccb211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x+2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329874} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c364a68-57f2-54a7-9b72-eaa196ce06be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7423fd02-a062-5332-9ecb-3b402fa82521" :question/math-academy-id "q-317583" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+0y=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b892e562-d61b-5d20-b4a3-5c1723f45300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329877} {:answer/id #uuid "b0122027-055d-5d98-9685-e7edbce56244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329878} {:answer/id #uuid "c4f411d6-8a60-58e9-a75b-20342550f565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329879} {:answer/id #uuid "c1494283-caa9-5450-b0e9-6820010095aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329880} {:answer/id #uuid "7f363274-ecf1-5e9e-96fe-cdf3be967f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1494283-caa9-5450-b0e9-6820010095aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329880} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2247b48-2570-5bf3-ba4a-0a47b98566e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c33f373f-cf05-5b2d-8a7f-abbee399267b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71800" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=7 \\\\ x+y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation, all the variables are on the left-hand side, and all the constants are on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=7 \\\\ x+y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce2e21aa-f89d-5d10-b815-c66a2b46ef5c" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a 2x2 System of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44ed27e5-22a4-58c6-aa20-729a2fe72fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329884} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9f6771-161c-534c-8c95-8edbb3140235" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329885} {:answer/id #uuid "f65c4c55-97a5-5f3b-ae2c-a8a3173c0cf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329886} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc385d0-76dc-524e-a9af-4d396c0b4ab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329887} {:answer/id #uuid "3c36d94a-4237-5fa9-be85-009851852af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a9f6771-161c-534c-8c95-8edbb3140235" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329885} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae9e8a3d-8cfb-594b-8891-1ea6b2009fbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "435e7026-e394-50fd-9cc2-55c6f6298c7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71804" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y=-1 \\\\ 5x=15\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. \nThe variable $y$ does not appear in the second equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y=-1 \\\\ 5x+0y=15\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe2300a1-f31e-5a24-889a-6f45e1e8647b" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Matrix Product as a 2x2 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f72e51d0-3003-5eb2-bad4-691761ef852e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ x-4y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329891} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9bbbef-46ca-574d-b4c6-0a2912ac6aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ -4x+y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329892} {:answer/id #uuid "6a6d2f86-9a9a-5d92-80c7-152d8d20dab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ x-4y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329893} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c4b04d-cd8c-59ce-81d6-4bca3f3dcacd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=5 \\\\ x-4y=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329894} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a6a7b2-71e1-5b75-8ace-303392b410b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ x-3y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f72e51d0-3003-5eb2-bad4-691761ef852e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ x-4y=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329891} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a539e03-7dd8-5ed0-882b-b1111dc9cfab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f74fa12-0053-502d-b17f-669ab25e05d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-71854" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x-y=0 \\\\ -3x+12y=-15.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=0 \\\\ x-4y=5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
